      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/6089a594bb0b0500707c78d8/e0c89ba4-1407-406d-af50-dc665f216277/16",
       "24x24": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/6089a594bb0b0500707c78d8/e0c89ba4-1407-406d-af50-dc665f216277/24",
       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/6089a594bb0b0500707c78d8/e0c89ba4-1407-406d-af50-dc665f216277/32",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/6089a594bb0b0500707c78d8/e0c89ba4-1407-406d-af50-dc665f216277/48"
      },
      "displayName": "Dan Field",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a594bb0b0500707c78d8",
      "timeZone": "Europe/London"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "We could perhaps add an additional CLI argument to sit alongside  the current pidlist opt-in ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "type": "code"
           }
          ],
          "text": "-p",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": " argument, This argument would need to be mutually exclusive to ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "type": "code"
           }
          ],
          "text": "-p",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": " in order to make any sense though. I can not think of a use case for requirng both. ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "What I am less clear on, is how the wildcard functionality would work. Was there a specific use-case for this? Presumably it’s usefullness is dependant on the convention of a users PIDs. wildcards for UUIDs don’t make much sense but could perhaps be os use in sequential numeric PIDs or alpha-numeric PIDs. ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
